{"seq":14,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/claude-code-opus-gbrain-told-labelled-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T14:33:49.230Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"cef64086f55e24c9b821def041c59d72d7e4f25222530906bd5b208b66b5fd32","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all of Moss's notes (the six Moss digests in the shared team folders). Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers come up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers at Eau Claire Dock Doors 14–18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments at gatehouse kiosk check-in. Support patched it that evening and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct 04:00 shift cleared. There's also a follow-up item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. The note says it was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing.\n\nOne thing to check before it goes in the weekly notes: Marcus's handoff note from 14 Jul 2025 (members/marcus-lindqvist/notes/2025-07-14-marcus-q2-expansion-wrap.md, which isn't a Moss note) also lists #4419, but as \"Gate 3 printer lag\", a BOL printout delay. Either the cheat sheet or Marcus's note has the wrong description, so I'd confirm with Marcus or Support.\n\nThe other ticket numbers in Moss's notes aren't Quarrendon tickets: #4409, #4412 and FR-882 are Central accounts. I also left out Quarendon Freightways (one \"r\"). It's a different company and not a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
